#--: Overview

The declarations themselves live in #~"lib/system/math.z" and its
subunits under #~"lib/system/math/", which are the one place they are
written; every definition carries its own doc comment, and #~"zls"
surfaces each on hover. This page is the prose and the worked examples.

The #~"math" unit holds numbers past the machine's own. Today that is
#b:"BigInt", a signed integer of any size, #b:"BigRat", a rational of any
size, #b:"BigFloat", a binary floating-point number of any precision, and
the fixed-width integers #b:"int" and #b:"uint" of any number of 64-bit
words (#~"i256", #~"u256", #~"i512", #~"u512"), and the SQL #~"NUMERIC"
fixed decimals #b:"decimal32", #b:"decimal64", #b:"decimal128" and
#b:"decimal256", and #b:"float", a binary float of a fixed number of
mantissa words.

The core is a port of Go's #~"math/big" at commit #~"577b91f341"
(BSD-3-Clause, the license beside it in #~"math/LICENSE-GO"); each ported
file names the Go file it came from. The algorithms are Go's:
Karatsuba multiplication and squaring, Burnikel-Ziegler division,
divide-and-conquer conversion to text, windowed and Montgomery
exponentiation, Lehmer's GCD, and a Baillie-PSW primality test. Where
Go lets a result alias an operand, the port writes into a second list
or calls an in-place twin, and the scratch Go takes from a stack is
one list sized before the work starts and carved into windows.

#code language=zerolang: """
  main: function is {
      a: math.BigInt from: 9223372036854775807
      b: a * a * a
      print "\{b.string}"
      print "\{(b.text base: 16)}"
      r: math.BigInt.parse text: "-0x_dead_beef" base: 0
      match (r) case ok then print "\{r.string}" case err then print "bad"
  }
  """


#--: Index

#p: #b:"Types"

#ul:
  [#*: [#> to=bigint: #b:"BigInt"] -- #~"class { negative: bool  words: ListVal u64 }": a sign and a magnitude]
  [#*: [#> to=bigdivision: #b:"BigDivision"] -- #~"class { quo: BigInt  rem: BigInt }"]
  [#*: [#> to=biggcd: #b:"BigGCD"] -- #~"class { gcd: BigInt  x: BigInt  y: BigInt }"]
  [#*: [#> to=bigrat: #b:"BigRat"] -- #~"class { num: BigInt  den: BigInt }": a quotient in lowest terms]
  [#*: [#> to=decimalprec: #b:"decimalprec"] -- #~"record { digits: u64  exact: bool }"]
  [#*: [#> to=bigfloat: #b:"BigFloat"] -- #~"class { prec: u32  mode: roundingmode  acc: accuracy ... }": a binary float of any precision]
  [#*: [#> to=roundingmode: #b:"roundingmode"] -- #~"variant { toNearestEven  toNearestAway  toZero  awayFromZero  toNegativeInf  toPositiveInf }"]
  [#*: [#> to=accuracy: #b:"accuracy"] -- #~"variant { below  exact  above }"]
  [#*: [#> to=floatformat: #b:"floatformat"] -- #~"variant { exponent  exponentUpper  fixed  general  generalUpper  hex  hexFraction  binary }"]
  [#*: [#> to=fixed-binary-floats: #b:"float"] -- #~"record { negative  form  exp: i32  mant: (array u64 to: words) } as { words: u64.generic }": BigFloat's semantics at #~"64*words" bits, held inline]
  [#*: [#> to=fixed-decimals: #b:"decimal32", #b:"decimal64", #b:"decimal128", #b:"decimal256"] -- #~"record { coef } as { precision: u8.generic  scale: u8.generic }": #~"NUMERIC(precision, scale)" over 9, 18, 38 or 76 digits]
  [#*: [#> to=fixed-decimals: #b:"decerror"] -- #~"variant { overflow  divisionByZero }": why a decimal is invalid]
  [#*: [#> to=fixed-width-integers: #b:"int", #b:"uint"] -- #~"record { limbs: (array t: u64 to: words) } as { words: u64.generic }": a two's complement integer of #~"64*words" bits; #~"i256", #~"u256", #~"i512", #~"u512" name four]

